menu "Audio engine"

config AUDIO_SCRATCH_ENABLED
    bool "Enable vinyl/scratch mode (jog platter scratches the audio)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, touching the FLX4 jog platter top while a deck plays
        scratches the audio (forward + reverse) by driving a read head over the
        per-deck PSRAM scratch capture buffer, instead of the Phase 1 platter
        hold+scrub. Releasing seeks normal forward playback to the head position.
        Additive: with this off the output path is unchanged and touching the
        platter does the Phase 1 hold/scrub. See docs/VINYL_SCRATCH_PLAN.md.

config AUDIO_DISPLAY_LATENCY_MS
    int "Output latency past the UAC ring, for the displayed position (ms)"
    range 0 200
    default 18
    help
        The engine position counts frames when they are mixed; they become
        audible only after the output chain. The UI shows the position that
        was mixed this long ago: the measured UAC ring fill (smoothed, read
        by the UI) plus this constant, which covers the isoc URBs in flight
        (3 x 6 ms since v329, 3 x 4 ms before: default 12 then) and the
        controller's own buffering. v260 HB logs: ring
        ~830-1280 frames at 48 kHz (17-27 ms), so ~35 ms in total.
        Raise it if the waveform still leads the audio, 0 = ring only.

choice AUDIO_KEYLOCK_ALGO
    prompt "Master Tempo (key lock) algorithm"
    default AUDIO_KEYLOCK_WSOLA2
    help
        v326: WSOLA v2 (audio_keylock_wsola2.c) replaces the original WSOLA
        (audio_keylock.c): whole-frame grains of 32 ms with an 11 ms aligned
        crossfade, +/-10.7 ms normalised-correlation search, and the v325
        windowed-sinc rate conversion. v1 stays compiled as the fallback.
        v327: v2 on both decks by default. HIL v326 (P4 PROBE): v2 costs
        about 36 us per 16-frame group and deck, v1 about 50, so the A/B
        (v2 + v1) was the most expensive two-deck combination.

    config AUDIO_KEYLOCK_WSOLA1
        bool "WSOLA v1 on both decks (original)"
    config AUDIO_KEYLOCK_WSOLA2
        bool "WSOLA v2 on both decks"
    config AUDIO_KEYLOCK_AB_DECK1
        bool "A/B: WSOLA v2 on deck 1, v1 on deck 2"
        help
            Listening A/B: load the same track on both decks with Master
            Tempo on and the same tempo, and switch with the crossfader.
endchoice

endmenu
